$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=twingf  LOC_AFTER=?

* For J at most Z and coprime to twice the multiplier, the greatest common divisor of the sifting product with J is a given divisor L of the sifting product exactly when J and L have the same prime divisors.

